 static long gcd(long a,long b) { while(b!=0){long t=a%b;a=b;b=t;} return Math.abs(a); }\n  static long power(long a,long b,long m) {long r=1%m;while(b>0){if((b&1)==1)r=r*a%m;a=a*a%m;b>>=1;}return r;}\n  static String solve(FastScanner in) throws Exception {\nint n=in.nextInt(),k=in.nextInt();int[] a=array(in,n);long[] d=new long[k+1];d[0]=1;for(int x:a)for(int j=x;j<=k;j++)d[j]=(d[j]+d[j-x])%MOD;return \"\"+d[k];\n  }\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception { System.out.println(solve(new FastScanner())); }\n}\n","cases":[{"ordinal":1,"stdin":"3 5\n1 2 5\n","expected_output":"4","is_sample":true},{"ordinal":2,"stdin":"1 3\n2\n","expected_output":"0","is_sample":true},{"ordinal":3,"stdin":"1 0\n1\n","expected_output":"1","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":4,"stdin":"1 7\n1\n","expected_output":"1","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":5,"stdin":"3 12\n2 3 7\n","expected_output":"4","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":6,"stdin":"2 15\n3 5\n","expected_output":"2","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":7,"stdin":"2 7\n4 6\n","expected_output":"0","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":8,"stdin":"3 10\n1 3 4\n","expected_output":"8","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":9,"stdin":"4 60\n2 5 10 20\n","expected_output":"50","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":10,"stdin":"5 35\n1 2 3 4 5\n","expected_output":"1115","is_sample":false}]},{"slug":"convex-hull-doubled-area","title":"Convex Hull Doubled Area","prompt":"Print twice the area of the convex hull of the points. Duplicate points are allowed. Fewer than three noncollinear distinct points gives 0.\n\nInput\nn, then n lines x y. 1 <= n <= 2000; -1000000 <= x,y <= 1000000.\n\nRead standard input and print only the requested result. Array indices are zero-based. Use 64-bit integers for sums and counts unless stated otherwise.\n\nExample 1\nInput:\n5\n0 0\n2 0\n2 2\n0 2\n1 1\nOutput:\n8\n\nExample 2\nInput:\n3\n0 0\n1 1\n2 2\nOutput:\n0","difficulty":8,"starter_code":"\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\npublic class Main {\n  static final long MOD 