solve(FastScanner in) throws Exception {\nString s=in.next();int n=s.length();Deque<Integer>q=new ArrayDeque<>();q.push(-1);int best=0;for(int i=0;i<n;i++){if(s.charAt(i)==40)q.push(i);else{q.pop();if(q.isEmpty())q.push(i);else best=Math.max(best,i-q.peek());}}return \"\"+best;\n  }\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception { System.out.println(solve(new FastScanner())); }\n}\n","cases":[{"ordinal":1,"stdin":"())\n","expected_output":"2","is_sample":true},{"ordinal":2,"stdin":"(((\n","expected_output":"0","is_sample":true},{"ordinal":3,"stdin":")\n","expected_output":"0","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":4,"stdin":"(\n","expected_output":"0","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":5,"stdin":"()\n","expected_output":"2","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":6,"stdin":"((()))\n","expected_output":"6","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":7,"stdin":"(()\n","expected_output":"2","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":8,"stdin":"())(()\n","expected_output":"2","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":9,"stdin":"()()()\n","expected_output":"6","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":10,"stdin":"(((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((((()))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))\n","expected_output":"98","is_sample":false}]},{"slug":"longest-bitonic-subsequence","title":"Longest Bitonic Subsequence","prompt":"Print the longest subsequence length that first strictly increases and then strictly decreases. Either phase may have length zero.\n\nInput\nn followed by n nonnegative integers; 1 <= n <= 100, 0 <= a[i] <= 100.\n\nRead standard input and print only the requested result. Array indices are zero-based. Use 64-bit integers for sums and counts unless stated otherwise.\n\nExample 1\nInput:\n5\n2 7 9 3 1\nOutput:\n5\n\nExample 2\nInput:\n3\n1 2 3\nOutput:\n3","difficulty":7,"starter_code":"\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\npublic class Main {\n  static final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n  static class FastScanner {\n    private final InputStream in = System.in;\n    private final byte[] buffer = n