return j.toString();\n  }\n  static long gcd(long a,long b) { while(b!=0){long t=a%b;a=b;b=t;} return Math.abs(a); }\n  static long power(long a,long b,long m) {long r=1%m;while(b>0){if((b&1)==1)r=r*a%m;a=a*a%m;b>>=1;}return r;}\n  static String solve(FastScanner in) throws Exception {\nlong a=in.nextLong(),m=in.nextLong(),r0=a,r1=m,s0=1,s1=0;while(r1!=0){long q=r0/r1,t=r0-q*r1;r0=r1;r1=t;t=s0-q*s1;s0=s1;s1=t;}return \"\"+(r0==1?(s0%m+m)%m:-1);\n  }\n  public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception { System.out.println(solve(new FastScanner())); }\n}\n","cases":[{"ordinal":1,"stdin":"3 11\n","expected_output":"4","is_sample":true},{"ordinal":2,"stdin":"2 4\n","expected_output":"-1","is_sample":true},{"ordinal":3,"stdin":"1 2\n","expected_output":"1","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":4,"stdin":"0 7\n","expected_output":"-1","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":5,"stdin":"10 17\n","expected_output":"12","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":6,"stdin":"7 19\n","expected_output":"11","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":7,"stdin":"25 100\n","expected_output":"-1","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":8,"stdin":"17 3120\n","expected_output":"2753","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":9,"stdin":"12345 65537\n","expected_output":"31651","is_sample":false},{"ordinal":10,"stdin":"99991 1000000007\n","expected_output":"278145035","is_sample":false}]},{"slug":"monotone-binary-flips","title":"Monotone Binary Flips","prompt":"Print the minimum bit flips to make the string nondecreasing (all zeros before all ones). Either group may be empty.\n\nInput\nOne nonempty binary string, of length at most 2000.\n\nRead standard input and print only the requested result. Array indices are zero-based. Use 64-bit integers for sums and counts unless stated otherwise.\n\nExample 1\nInput:\n00110011\nOutput:\n2\n\nExample 2\nInput:\n0101\nOutput:\n1","difficulty":5,"starter_code":"\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\npublic class Main {\n  static final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n  static class FastScanner {\n    private fi